{
  "version": "0.1",
  "connections": [
    {
      "details": {
        "protocol": "google-bigquery",
        "address": {
          "project": "REPLACE_WITH_BIGQUERY_PROJECT_ID",
          "dataset": "REPLACE_WITH_BIGQUERY_DATASET"
        }
      },
      "mode": "DirectQuery"
    }
  ],
  "_comment": [
    "Power BI Data Source file (.pbids) -- open this in Power BI Desktop and it",
    "opens the Navigator already pointed at the tenant's BigQuery dataset in",
    "DirectQuery mode, so nobody has to retype the connection or accidentally",
    "pick Import and ship a stale snapshot.",
    "",
    "This is NOT the .pbix. A .pbix is a proprietary binary that only Power BI",
    "Desktop can author; see docs/analysis/2026-08-09-blocked-work-register.md.",
    "This file is the part that can be version-controlled, reviewed and diffed.",
    "",
    "Replace both REPLACE_WITH_ placeholders with the tenant's values -- they are",
    "settings.bigquery_project_id and settings.bigquery_dataset. Deliberately not",
    "pre-filled: this file is committed, and a real project id in the repo is a",
    "small invitation to point a report at the wrong tenant.",
    "",
    "DirectQuery, not Import, is the mode that matters. Import copies the data",
    "into the .pbix, so the report silently serves whatever was true at the last",
    "refresh -- which is exactly the failure the client raised at the 2026-07-28",
    "demo. See power-bi-runbook.md."
  ]
}
